1
00:00:01,953 --> 00:00:03,962
(A New Meeting)

2
00:00:03,963 --> 00:00:06,593
- Nice to see you all. - Nice to see you.

3
00:00:07,363 --> 00:00:09,702
Last week's preview went viral.

4
00:00:09,703 --> 00:00:11,663
- Even I got so excited for it. - Right.

5
00:00:11,933 --> 00:00:13,672
Team Chunk of our show got together.

6
00:00:13,673 --> 00:00:14,702
Wait, you mean us?

7
00:00:14,703 --> 00:00:16,202
- Team Chunk? - I saw that in a comment.

8
00:00:16,203 --> 00:00:18,002
- Did you just call us Team Chunk? - You're the Chunk Trio.

9
00:00:18,003 --> 00:00:19,012
I mean, it's fine for us.

10
00:00:19,013 --> 00:00:20,642
- You can't call her that. - Right.

11
00:00:20,643 --> 00:00:21,672
Just like HYORISOO,

12
00:00:21,673 --> 00:00:23,082
- I'll be the third member... - Yes.

13
00:00:23,083 --> 00:00:25,043
- The third member? - if I have to do it anyway.

14
00:00:25,113 --> 00:00:26,212
- I'm the heaviest. - He's the heaviest.

15
00:00:26,213 --> 00:00:27,483
- Second. Third. - Second. Third.

16
00:00:28,313 --> 00:00:29,523
He's definitely the leader.

17
00:00:29,983 --> 00:00:31,022
Right, he should be the leader.

18
00:00:31,023 --> 00:00:32,822
To me, they all look like they could be their own leader.

19
00:00:32,823 --> 00:00:33,823
- What do you mean? - Hey.

20
00:00:34,423 --> 00:00:36,122
- How dare you say that to her? - I'll be the lightest member.

21
00:00:36,123 --> 00:00:37,123
- I'm the lightest member. - How could you?

22
00:00:37,124 --> 00:00:38,522
- The heaviest and the lightest. - I'm the lightest.

23
00:00:38,523 --> 00:00:39,893
- The heaviest and the lightest. - The heaviest and the lightest.

24
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:42,433
- It will be a delicious segment. - Definitely.

25
00:00:42,803 --> 00:00:45,402
I want our viewers to eat something before watching our episode.

26
00:00:45,403 --> 00:00:46,702
- Is that really necessary? - They might get gastric acid.

27
00:00:46,703 --> 00:00:47,802
- Gastric acid? - Something like that.

28
00:00:47,803 --> 00:00:49,602
- Yes. - That's why I had triangle gimbap.

29
00:00:49,603 --> 00:00:52,103
(That's why I had triangle gimbap.)

30
00:00:52,573 --> 00:00:55,613
(How to Eat and Live Well)

31
00:00:56,743 --> 00:00:57,813
It's the heaviest member.

32
00:00:57,943 --> 00:00:59,383
Our dear heaviest member.

33
00:00:59,813 --> 00:01:01,213
I'm a regular at this butcher shop.

34
00:01:03,253 --> 00:01:06,153
My gosh. It's my first time watching you work.

35
00:01:06,923 --> 00:01:08,522
The thing I asked for yesterday...

36
00:01:08,523 --> 00:01:09,922
- arrived today. - Yes.

37
00:01:09,923 --> 00:01:12,123
Why are you wearing a matching outfit to the meat?

38
00:01:12,693 --> 00:01:13,732
- Hey. - It could've caused...

39
00:01:13,733 --> 00:01:14,793
a huge misunderstanding.

40
00:01:15,193 --> 00:01:17,263
- You almost got butchered. - Seriously.

41
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:19,403
I'm pork, and that's beef!

42
00:01:20,203 --> 00:01:21,203
(Don't confuse the two!)

43
00:01:21,204 --> 00:01:22,232
Seriously.

44
00:01:22,233 --> 00:01:24,243
- He got a chuck flap tail pattern. - Right.

45
00:01:25,143 --> 00:01:26,743
- He must be chuck flap tail. - I really want to grill you.

46
00:01:27,073 --> 00:01:28,443
(Come on, what kind of joke is that?)

47
00:01:28,773 --> 00:01:30,642
I bet it's really good grilled.

48
00:01:30,643 --> 00:01:32,213
It was delivered fresh from Eumseong.

49
00:01:33,213 --> 00:01:35,753
When did you get this meat then?

50
00:01:36,323 --> 00:01:37,783
We bought it at an auction yesterday.

51
00:01:37,883 --> 00:01:39,552
- Just yesterday? - It was processed then.

52
00:01:39,553 --> 00:01:40,752
(It's fresh from yesterday's auction.)

53
00:01:40,753 --> 00:01:41,793
- Really? - Yes.

54
00:01:42,863 --> 00:01:44,422
It's got the freshest color.

55
00:01:44,423 --> 00:01:45,793
(It's got the freshest color.)

56
00:01:46,693 --> 00:01:48,263
(Salivating)

57
00:01:48,593 --> 00:01:50,032
Does your mouth water just by looking at that?

58
00:01:50,033 --> 00:01:51,532
- Let me explain. - People rarely salivate...

59
00:01:51,533 --> 00:01:53,133
- when they see raw meat. - Listen.

60
00:01:53,603 --> 00:01:55,532
What are you talking about? Check out that color.

61
00:01:55,533 --> 00:01:57,172
- Of course. - Once you grill it...

62
00:01:57,173 --> 00:01:59,843
Only lions drool when they see raw meat like that.

63
00:02:00,873 --> 00:02:03,113
- Hey, you! - I'm so sorry.

64
00:02:03,383 --> 00:02:04,942
- You're one of us. - Hey, be careful.

65
00:02:04,943 --> 00:02:06,053
- I'll be careful. - You have to be careful.

66
00:02:06,513 --> 00:02:08,853
(I'll be careful.)

67
00:02:09,683 --> 00:02:11,682
(Carefully watching him butcher it while drooling)

68
00:02:11,683 --> 00:02:13,493
The color definitely looks different.

69
00:02:16,463 --> 00:02:17,922
My brother.

70
00:02:17,923 --> 00:02:19,393
(My brother)

71
00:02:19,533 --> 00:02:20,832
- Hey, Seon Min. - My brother.

72
00:02:20,833 --> 00:02:22,133
- Gosh, you came right away. - I did.

73
00:02:23,233 --> 00:02:24,233
Gosh, what's this?

74
00:02:24,234 --> 00:02:25,802
- Hello. - You know who he is, right?

75
00:02:25,803 --> 00:02:27,273
- "My brother." - It's Min.

76
00:02:27,503 --> 00:02:29,803
The best comedian, Min, came.

77
00:02:30,673 --> 00:02:32,473
We all went to a summer retreat a while ago.

78
00:02:32,613 --> 00:02:35,613
He kept giving me the look.

79
00:02:35,913 --> 00:02:38,413
At that moment, I sensed that...

80
00:02:38,783 --> 00:02:41,413
he and I would get along well like good brothers.

81
00:02:42,313 --> 00:02:45,383
(The two of them met as the same team, "Between Power and Ham.")

82
00:02:45,923 --> 00:02:50,363
(As they joined hands and worked together,)

83
00:02:51,723 --> 00:02:53,392
(their team won the game.)

84
00:02:53,393 --> 00:02:54,692
We bonded...

85
00:02:54,693 --> 00:02:56,432
- when we were on the same team. - Totally.

86
00:02:56,433 --> 00:02:57,702
- We bonded deeply. - Yes.

87
00:02:57,703 --> 00:02:58,863
It's Chobok.

88
00:02:58,933 --> 00:03:00,573
To celebrate Chobok,

89
00:03:01,003 --> 00:03:03,842
I invited close friends of mine to my place.

90
00:03:03,843 --> 00:03:06,713
So I was there to get some high-quality ingredients.

91
00:03:07,713 --> 00:03:09,743
I invited them because it was Chobok.

92
00:03:10,143 --> 00:03:11,313
- To have invigorating food? - Yes.

93
00:03:11,713 --> 00:03:14,553
- Seeing you in my neighborhood... - Yes.

94
00:03:15,013 --> 00:03:16,882
- makes me so happy. - I'm happy to be here too.

95
00:03:16,883 --> 00:03:18,423
- Let me explain. - On my way here...

96
00:03:18,553 --> 00:03:20,923
I'm the honorary ambassador of Gangdong-gu.

97
00:03:21,423 --> 00:03:22,822
- For real? - Yes.

98
00:03:22,823 --> 00:03:26,033
I'm the honorary ambassador of Gangdong-gu.

99
00:03:26,293 --> 00:03:28,593
I asked him to prepare this cut of meat a few days in advance.

100
00:03:29,133 --> 00:03:30,432
It's my favorite cut.

101
00:03:30,433 --> 00:03:32,003
(I set this up, so I could feed you the good-quality meat.)

102
00:03:32,263 --> 00:03:34,032
(Amazed)

103
00:03:34,033 --> 00:03:35,203
I can't wait to try it.

104
00:03:36,173 --> 00:03:37,603
Do you want to try it raw to refresh your palate?

105
00:03:38,173 --> 00:03:39,173
Sounds good.

106
00:03:39,343 --> 00:03:41,112
You don't get that kind of service...

107
00:03:41,113 --> 00:03:42,143
- unless you're a real regular. - Right.

108
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:44,313
- Just with some salt? - Wait.

109
00:03:45,043 --> 00:03:46,853
- You're in Gangdong-gu. - Yes.

110
00:03:46,983 --> 00:03:48,583
- You try it first. - My gosh.

111
00:03:49,013 --> 00:03:50,582
- Try that. - Thank you.

112
00:03:50,583 --> 00:03:51,583
(He dips it in salt...)

113
00:03:51,584 --> 00:03:53,253
(and eats it in one bite.)

114
00:03:56,263 --> 00:03:57,323
Isn't it good?

115
00:03:58,393 --> 00:03:59,962
- Isn't it good? - It's super fresh.

116
00:03:59,963 --> 00:04:01,033
Okay. Great.

117
00:04:01,433 --> 00:04:02,632
Gosh, it's the freshest meat ever.

118
00:04:02,633 --> 00:04:03,933
(Feeling proud)

119
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:05,333
Gosh, it's the freshest meat ever.

120
00:04:06,673 --> 00:04:07,803
What's going on?

121
00:04:08,633 --> 00:04:09,702
You should try it too.

122
00:04:09,703 --> 00:04:11,442
- You know what? - Come on.

123
00:04:11,443 --> 00:04:13,042
- No. - I'm fine.

124
00:04:13,043 --> 00:04:14,242
- You should try it too. - No.

125
00:04:14,243 --> 00:04:15,782
- Sung Hwan. - I'll have it grilled later.

126
00:04:15,783 --> 00:04:17,082
- No. You must try it. - Gosh, no.

127
00:04:17,083 --> 00:04:19,513
Here's the thing. I love it too.

128
00:04:19,683 --> 00:04:22,413
I have a very weak stomach. I must dip it in some sauce.

129
00:04:22,553 --> 00:04:23,623
Sung Hwan.

130
00:04:24,053 --> 00:04:25,282
- I didn't think you were that weak. - Seon Min.

131
00:04:25,283 --> 00:04:26,322
No. I have a weak stomach.

132
00:04:26,323 --> 00:04:28,453
I like staying at hotels. I don't like going camping.

133
00:04:28,953 --> 00:04:29,962
That's where I lean toward.

134
00:04:29,963 --> 00:04:32,022
Sung Hwan does have a weak stomach.

135
00:04:32,023 --> 00:04:33,692
I see. You can't even eat raw beef?

136
00:04:33,693 --> 00:04:36,462
You have to understand that I have a weak stomach...

137
00:04:36,463 --> 00:04:37,703
despite how I look.

138
00:04:38,103 --> 00:04:40,333
- It was freshly butchered. - I thought you were a cool guy.

139
00:04:40,673 --> 00:04:42,873
- It was freshly butchered. - I thought you were a cool guy.

140
00:04:43,473 --> 00:04:45,103
- I thought you were a cool guy. - Look at his eyes.

141
00:04:45,273 --> 00:04:46,572
You ought to try it.

142
00:04:46,573 --> 00:04:47,713
(Grabbing)

143
00:04:48,013 --> 00:04:49,612
My gosh. This looks good.

144
00:04:49,613 --> 00:04:51,643
(Yes, I'm a cool guy.)

145
00:04:51,983 --> 00:04:53,052
Isn't it good?

146
00:04:53,053 --> 00:04:55,983
(Isn't it good?)

147
00:04:56,423 --> 00:04:57,423
(Humming)

148
00:04:59,193 --> 00:05:00,822
Yes, it was tasty.

149
00:05:00,823 --> 00:05:02,763
I didn't know you were a picky eater.

150
00:05:02,893 --> 00:05:04,363
- He's very picky about food. - It's...

151
00:05:05,293 --> 00:05:06,433
- Right? - It's nice.

152
00:05:07,033 --> 00:05:08,332
Come on, lighten up.

153
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:09,333
(Teary-eyed)

154
00:05:09,334 --> 00:05:10,833
- Thank you. - Gosh, sir.

155
00:05:11,303 --> 00:05:12,633
You have the freshest meat.

156
00:05:13,103 --> 00:05:14,173
Gosh, the meat is so fresh today.

157
00:05:14,933 --> 00:05:17,502
(He purchases the freshly butchered meat.)

158
00:05:17,503 --> 00:05:18,573
I feel rich.

159
00:05:18,773 --> 00:05:20,013
It's 410 dollars.

160
00:05:20,613 --> 00:05:22,143
- What? - What?

161
00:05:22,513 --> 00:05:24,913
My people were coming over. I had to treat them to a nice meal.

162
00:05:24,983 --> 00:05:26,783
- Hwan is super cool. - Are you sure about this?

163
00:05:27,053 --> 00:05:29,353
Come on. I'm the honorary ambassador of Gangdong-gu!

164
00:05:29,523 --> 00:05:31,022
Is that a paying position?

165
00:05:31,023 --> 00:05:32,153
No.

166
00:05:32,553 --> 00:05:34,252
- It's an honorary position. - I'm just an honorary ambassador.

167
00:05:34,253 --> 00:05:35,352
It's an honorary position.

168
00:05:35,353 --> 00:05:36,762
(The honorary ambassador buys meat for his good friend.)

169
00:05:36,763 --> 00:05:38,193
- Bye. - Thank you.

170
00:05:38,293 --> 00:05:39,533
- Okay. - Bye.

171
00:05:39,633 --> 00:05:41,063
- I won't see you off. - Okay.

172
00:05:41,393 --> 00:05:43,232
- Shouldn't he be saying that? - That's...

173
00:05:43,233 --> 00:05:45,063
That's my thing.

174
00:05:45,733 --> 00:05:47,473
- "I won't see you off." - That's my signature line.

175
00:05:47,773 --> 00:05:50,473
- Since we're in Gangdong-gu, - Yes.

176
00:05:51,043 --> 00:05:53,172
I'll show you around.

177
00:05:53,173 --> 00:05:54,713
- Gosh, this feels different. - It does, right?

178
00:05:55,883 --> 00:05:57,713
- Welcome to Gangdong. - Oh, my.

179
00:05:57,813 --> 00:05:59,613
This place is huge.

180
00:05:59,683 --> 00:06:00,713
It's different, right?

181
00:06:01,813 --> 00:06:02,953
I love this market.

182
00:06:05,053 --> 00:06:06,152
Smell that.

183
00:06:06,153 --> 00:06:07,992
(Invigorating dishes are everywhere as it's Chobok.)

184
00:06:07,993 --> 00:06:09,093
That looks delicious.

185
00:06:09,323 --> 00:06:10,893
(The market has seasonal seafood...)

186
00:06:11,323 --> 00:06:13,363
(as well as seasonal fruits.)

187
00:06:13,493 --> 00:06:15,462
All right. We need to buy a few things.

188
00:06:15,463 --> 00:06:16,463
(Let's buy some groceries while we look around.)

189
00:06:16,703 --> 00:06:19,402
I got hwachae. Then I need tofu, green onion kimchi...

190
00:06:19,403 --> 00:06:21,773
- Are you opening a Korean buffet? - Gosh, no.

191
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:23,873
- Hold on. We need to... - Gosh, I love this market.

192
00:06:25,073 --> 00:06:26,243
- What do we need to buy? - Hello.

193
00:06:27,043 --> 00:06:28,542
- I'll get green onion kimchi. - Gosh.

194
00:06:28,543 --> 00:06:29,813
- That's... - Right from the market.

195
00:06:29,913 --> 00:06:31,083
- Nice. - How much?

196
00:06:31,343 --> 00:06:32,883
Thank you. Put it in the basket.

197
00:06:33,283 --> 00:06:35,182
- This looks authentic. - Their tofu is so good.

198
00:06:35,183 --> 00:06:36,523
- Is it handmade tofu? - Yes, it is.

199
00:06:37,123 --> 00:06:38,923
- Thank you. - Let me carry this.

200
00:06:39,123 --> 00:06:40,252
- Thank you. - Enjoy.

201
00:06:40,253 --> 00:06:41,322
- Thank you. - Sell a lot.

202
00:06:41,323 --> 00:06:42,423
Thank you.

203
00:06:42,593 --> 00:06:43,692
How nice.

204
00:06:43,693 --> 00:06:45,192
(Min and Hwan fill up the grocery bag.)

205
00:06:45,193 --> 00:06:46,392
I love it.

206
00:06:46,393 --> 00:06:48,132
- Let's get some brunch. - Yes.

207
00:06:48,133 --> 00:06:50,363
My favorite snack bar is here.

208
00:06:50,463 --> 00:06:52,503
- Snack food? That sounds good. - Yes. Let's eat something simple.

209
00:06:52,833 --> 00:06:55,173
- We can't eat a lot here because... - Something simple?

210
00:06:55,603 --> 00:06:57,973
we're going to get about three appetizers.

211
00:06:58,173 --> 00:06:59,472
Three appetizers?

212
00:06:59,473 --> 00:07:01,212
We're getting three appetizers.

213
00:07:01,213 --> 00:07:02,413
That's the one.

214
00:07:03,413 --> 00:07:05,043
- This is the place? - No, the one in front.

215
00:07:06,213 --> 00:07:07,483
I love this place.

216
00:07:07,853 --> 00:07:09,682
- A long time ago... - When I came back from Kazakhstan,

217
00:07:09,683 --> 00:07:11,653
- that was the first place I hit up. - I see.

218
00:07:11,953 --> 00:07:12,992
- After coming back to Korea? - With Ju Seung?

219
00:07:12,993 --> 00:07:14,052
Yes, I went there with Ju Seung.

220
00:07:14,053 --> 00:07:15,692
- My stomach is shrinking. - Oh, this episode?

221
00:07:15,693 --> 00:07:16,693
(He went with Ju Seung.)

222
00:07:17,023 --> 00:07:19,693
(The regular snack bar of the Gangdong-gu honorary ambassador)

223
00:07:20,163 --> 00:07:22,833
- Sir, I'm here. - Hello.

224
00:07:23,133 --> 00:07:24,502
- I'm here too. - Hello.

225
00:07:24,503 --> 00:07:27,072
- Nice to meet you. - He's visiting Gangdong-gu today.

226
00:07:27,073 --> 00:07:30,043
He bragged so much about this place. He said your food was amazing.

227
00:07:30,703 --> 00:07:31,902
I'm the honorary ambassador of Gangdong-gu.

228
00:07:31,903 --> 00:07:33,543
(Bowing)

229
00:07:33,643 --> 00:07:35,942
- This is our appetizer spot. - Okay.

230
00:07:35,943 --> 00:07:37,382
One fried squid, one gimmari,

231
00:07:37,383 --> 00:07:38,943
- and one fried pepper. - Fried squid?

232
00:07:39,453 --> 00:07:41,652
- I want you to try this tteokbokki. - Okay.

233
00:07:41,653 --> 00:07:43,553
Once you try it, you see how thick and gooey this is.

234
00:07:43,783 --> 00:07:45,523
- I love this kind of tteokbokki. - Let's put it down.

235
00:07:46,093 --> 00:07:47,823
- It's rice-based tteokbokki. - It is.

236
00:07:48,653 --> 00:07:49,892
That's the authentic tteokbokki.

237
00:07:49,893 --> 00:07:51,192
It's tastier...

238
00:07:51,193 --> 00:07:52,493
- when the sauce is thick like that. - Of course.

239
00:07:53,363 --> 00:07:54,462
You try it first.

240
00:07:54,463 --> 00:07:55,492
- Me? - Go ahead.

241
00:07:55,493 --> 00:07:57,062
He's a guest in my town. He must try it first.

242
00:07:57,063 --> 00:07:58,702
He always looks after Seon Min...

243
00:07:58,703 --> 00:08:00,373
- first. - Right.

244
00:08:04,443 --> 00:08:05,542
It's no joke, right?

245
00:08:05,543 --> 00:08:06,573
(Hugging)

246
00:08:06,973 --> 00:08:08,513
Gosh, this is so good.

247
00:08:08,743 --> 00:08:10,413
It's the perfect level of spiciness for me.

248
00:08:11,083 --> 00:08:12,183
- Right. - It's nice and spicy.

249
00:08:12,313 --> 00:08:14,682
- It's thick, spicy, - Gosh, that looks good.

250
00:08:14,683 --> 00:08:17,083
- and chewy. - It's super thick.

251
00:08:17,253 --> 00:08:18,523
Rice-based tteokbokki must be nice and thick.

252
00:08:19,053 --> 00:08:21,122
The rice cakes have to get stuck on your front teeth.

253
00:08:21,123 --> 00:08:22,552
- That's exactly it. - It has to be a sticky bite.

254
00:08:22,553 --> 00:08:23,923
- You're spot on. - Right.

255
00:08:24,523 --> 00:08:27,392
- Finish the last piece. - Can I have that luxury?

256
00:08:27,393 --> 00:08:28,463
Go ahead.

257
00:08:31,563 --> 00:08:32,872
(Scraping)

258
00:08:32,873 --> 00:08:34,803
- There you go. That hits the spot. - Gosh. Hey, you...

259
00:08:35,233 --> 00:08:38,003
- Gosh. Hey, you... - This is it.

260
00:08:38,173 --> 00:08:39,813
You know how to enjoy food.

261
00:08:40,243 --> 00:08:42,512
- I had to finish the sauce too. - Exactly. You must eat it up.

262
00:08:42,513 --> 00:08:44,842
(He scrapes the sauce and eats it up.)

263
00:08:44,843 --> 00:08:46,382
- I'll share a useful tip. - Tell us.

264
00:08:46,383 --> 00:08:47,953
They cover the plate with the plastic bag.

265
00:08:48,053 --> 00:08:50,523
Grab the plastic bag and squeeze out the sauce.

266
00:08:50,783 --> 00:08:53,422
- Then it ends up in a triangle. - Like a piping bag.

267
00:08:53,423 --> 00:08:55,123
Treat it like a piping bag.

268
00:08:55,393 --> 00:08:57,593
Tear it open with your nail and squeeze out the sauce.

269
00:08:57,893 --> 00:08:59,063
- Like a freezie? - Yes.

270
00:08:59,323 --> 00:09:00,662
It's really good...

271
00:09:00,663 --> 00:09:01,992
- It was so good. - when you squeeze out the sauce.

272
00:09:01,993 --> 00:09:03,263
(Make sure to eat every drop of the sauce.)

273
00:09:03,533 --> 00:09:05,033
Gosh, we're off to a great start.

274
00:09:05,803 --> 00:09:06,903
Goodness, it was good.

275
00:09:07,833 --> 00:09:09,033
It was perfect.

276
00:09:10,073 --> 00:09:11,403
- Let me pay for this. - Come on.

277
00:09:11,903 --> 00:09:12,943
Don't.

278
00:09:13,713 --> 00:09:14,973
I hate it when my people do that.

279
00:09:15,273 --> 00:09:16,383
- Come on. - No!

280
00:09:16,843 --> 00:09:18,682
- Sung Hwan. - I'm sorry. Don't make me yell.

281
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:19,812
Gosh, you're...

282
00:09:19,813 --> 00:09:21,052
I can't allow that.

283
00:09:21,053 --> 00:09:22,153
Sung Hwan.

284
00:09:22,283 --> 00:09:25,983
He doesn't let his juniors spend money in Gangdong-gu.

285
00:09:27,423 --> 00:09:29,562
Sung Hwan. Thank you for the food.

286
00:09:29,563 --> 00:09:31,263
How much is it?

287
00:09:32,163 --> 00:09:33,633
It's seven dollars.

288
00:09:34,563 --> 00:09:36,563
- It didn't even cost that much. - Hey.

289
00:09:37,203 --> 00:09:39,003
- Hold on. - I thought it was 70 dollars.

290
00:09:39,503 --> 00:09:40,503
- I wanted to pay... - That's...

291
00:09:40,504 --> 00:09:41,572
- because it was only seven dollars. - No, listen.

292
00:09:41,573 --> 00:09:42,632
You're making a big deal out of it.

293
00:09:42,633 --> 00:09:43,642
He made it sound like the meal cost 700 dollars.

294
00:09:43,643 --> 00:09:44,643
Exactly.

295
00:09:44,644 --> 00:09:46,443
- "No!" - Listen.

296
00:09:46,973 --> 00:09:49,913
- This is so embarrassing. - My face is getting red.

297
00:09:50,913 --> 00:09:52,513
- But you were still cool. - Really?

298
00:09:52,643 --> 00:09:53,783
That's really cheap.

299
00:09:54,153 --> 00:09:55,752
(He pays 7 dollars like a cool guy.)

300
00:09:55,753 --> 00:09:56,882
It was so good.

301
00:09:56,883 --> 00:10:00,692
I enjoyed your food once again.

302
00:10:00,693 --> 00:10:01,723
Thank you.

303
00:10:02,093 --> 00:10:03,793
I saw him and his parents on TV.

304
00:10:04,393 --> 00:10:05,423
Thank you.

305
00:10:05,663 --> 00:10:08,332
Out of all the comedians,

306
00:10:08,333 --> 00:10:10,502
his popularity among people in their 20s and 30s is...

307
00:10:10,503 --> 00:10:11,732
- He's the best. - the best.

308
00:10:11,733 --> 00:10:13,002
(Smiling)

309
00:10:13,003 --> 00:10:14,133
The young worker knows Seon Min.

310
00:10:14,673 --> 00:10:16,372
It feels good when you bring a junior...

311
00:10:16,373 --> 00:10:18,042
- It's a different feeling. - and they recognize you.

312
00:10:18,043 --> 00:10:19,072
Right.

313
00:10:19,073 --> 00:10:20,813
- We'll get going. - An autograph? Sure.

314
00:10:21,543 --> 00:10:23,783
- Make it look cool. - Gosh, Seon Min.

315
00:10:25,143 --> 00:10:26,783
(Here you go.)

316
00:10:27,553 --> 00:10:29,182
This is a charming piece of paper.

317
00:10:29,183 --> 00:10:30,852
- Here in Gangdong-gu... - Right on the take-out paper.

318
00:10:30,853 --> 00:10:32,783
- No. Here in my town... - The take-out paper...

319
00:10:32,953 --> 00:10:34,893
- It's like that here. Hey. - Look.

320
00:10:35,493 --> 00:10:36,723
- That's the way to go at markets. - How charming.

321
00:10:36,823 --> 00:10:38,122
It's the signature paper.

322
00:10:38,123 --> 00:10:39,963
- I actually liked that. - You did. Right? Yes.

323
00:10:40,193 --> 00:10:41,993
- When would you get this chance? - They'll frame it later.

324
00:10:43,133 --> 00:10:45,402
(Adding Sung Hwan's name)

325
00:10:45,403 --> 00:10:46,903
"With Ku Sung Hwan."

326
00:10:46,973 --> 00:10:48,933
(Gosh, Min...)

327
00:10:49,203 --> 00:10:50,902
- Thank you. - Thank you.

328
00:10:50,903 --> 00:10:52,743
- I'll come back. - See you next time.

329
00:10:52,873 --> 00:10:56,383
(They fill up their stomach in a good mood.)

330
00:10:57,413 --> 00:10:59,243
- Do you like sikhye? - Yes, I do.

331
00:11:00,053 --> 00:11:02,353
Drinking sikhye washes down heavy, dense food.

332
00:11:02,583 --> 00:11:04,223
- Really? - Of course.

333
00:11:04,483 --> 00:11:06,152
Does sikhye help with digestion?

334
00:11:06,153 --> 00:11:07,622
- Of course. It's got rice grains. - Not at all.

335
00:11:07,623 --> 00:11:09,392
- No? - Come on. "Not at all?"

336
00:11:09,393 --> 00:11:10,393
It helps digest food.

337
00:11:10,394 --> 00:11:11,722
Why do you think I drink Coke Zero?

338
00:11:11,723 --> 00:11:13,063
He's forcing the food to go down.

339
00:11:13,163 --> 00:11:15,863
- It just feels like that? - He's washing it down.

340
00:11:16,163 --> 00:11:18,303
(I like sikhye.)

341
00:11:18,903 --> 00:11:21,573
- Hello. - Sir, we'll take sikhye.

342
00:11:21,673 --> 00:11:22,803
- Sikhye? - Yes.

343
00:11:23,673 --> 00:11:24,742
"Digestive medicine."

344
00:11:24,743 --> 00:11:26,712
That's natural digestive medicine. I'm serious.

345
00:11:26,713 --> 00:11:28,272
- It's natural digestive medicine. - It's my first time hearing it.

346
00:11:28,273 --> 00:11:29,343
No. I'm serious.

347
00:11:31,383 --> 00:11:32,982
My gosh. Thank you, sir.

348
00:11:32,983 --> 00:11:35,112
- I'll carry this. - Thank you.

349
00:11:35,113 --> 00:11:36,323
- Okay. - Okay. Have a good day.

350
00:11:36,483 --> 00:11:37,582
Can I get an autograph?

351
00:11:37,583 --> 00:11:38,783
An autograph? Sure.

352
00:11:39,593 --> 00:11:41,093
- Gosh, another one. - On my phone, please.

353
00:11:41,893 --> 00:11:42,922
On your phone?

354
00:11:42,923 --> 00:11:44,123
Gosh, on his phone?

355
00:11:44,323 --> 00:11:46,762
- Goodness. I... - After starring on our show...

356
00:11:46,763 --> 00:11:47,993
People loved Seon Min.

357
00:11:48,693 --> 00:11:50,063
- That's crazy. - You can't throw it out.

358
00:11:50,333 --> 00:11:52,102
- Seon Min, you're super popular. - Right.

359
00:11:52,103 --> 00:11:53,172
I was very grateful.

360
00:11:53,173 --> 00:11:54,433
- That's... - Ho Young?

361
00:11:54,703 --> 00:11:56,472
- How old are you? - I'm 23.

362
00:11:56,473 --> 00:11:58,643
Yes. People in their 20s...

363
00:11:59,273 --> 00:12:00,972
- love Seon Min. - Unbalanced arms.

364
00:12:00,973 --> 00:12:03,043
My gosh. Thank you so much.

365
00:12:03,913 --> 00:12:04,913
(He hands over the autographed phone.)

366
00:12:04,914 --> 00:12:06,212
Thank you. One more?

367
00:12:06,213 --> 00:12:08,383
- Yes. - Do you sell phones here?

368
00:12:08,753 --> 00:12:10,223
My gosh, Seon Min.

369
00:12:10,753 --> 00:12:13,092
He must have multiple phones.

370
00:12:13,093 --> 00:12:14,792
The lady in the back wanted it too.

371
00:12:14,793 --> 00:12:16,593
It's impossible for Seon Min to walk around.

372
00:12:18,963 --> 00:12:21,532
At that moment, I remembered seeing him...

373
00:12:21,533 --> 00:12:23,333
in the Buzz outfit.

374
00:12:23,863 --> 00:12:25,203
- That was a critical moment. - Yes.

375
00:12:25,763 --> 00:12:27,503
- Seriously. - That was his career crisis.

376
00:12:27,603 --> 00:12:31,143
When CODE KUNST said Andy was there,

377
00:12:31,903 --> 00:12:33,713
I had some doubt about him.

378
00:12:36,243 --> 00:12:37,713
I vividly remember the look on Sung Hwan's face.

379
00:12:39,243 --> 00:12:40,782
(Gazing)

380
00:12:40,783 --> 00:12:41,853
The look on his face.

381
00:12:42,283 --> 00:12:43,753
- What's that? - Sung Hwan!

382
00:12:43,923 --> 00:12:45,682
- No! - I didn't see that.

383
00:12:45,683 --> 00:12:46,723
No.

384
00:12:47,793 --> 00:12:49,792
After seeing him at the market today...

385
00:12:49,793 --> 00:12:51,023
(He had some doubt about Min after the talent show.)

386
00:12:51,223 --> 00:12:52,893
I was quite surprised...

387
00:12:53,263 --> 00:12:55,633
because the younger generation recognized him.

388
00:12:56,093 --> 00:12:58,362
I saw how popular he was at the market today.

389
00:12:58,363 --> 00:12:59,632
(He saw Min's class at the market.)

390
00:12:59,633 --> 00:13:00,703
He's impressive.

391
00:13:01,603 --> 00:13:04,603
- It was crazy. - Getting recognized at markets...

392
00:13:04,973 --> 00:13:07,972
- makes you feel you're popular now. - Right.

393
00:13:07,973 --> 00:13:10,713
People went crazy at the market. Seriously. To people in their 20s,

394
00:13:10,913 --> 00:13:12,712
- he's like Seo Taiji. - Seriously.

395
00:13:12,713 --> 00:13:14,952
(To people in their 20s, he's like Seo Taiji.)

396
00:13:14,953 --> 00:13:16,083
My gosh.

397
00:13:16,753 --> 00:13:18,222
- Seon Min. - Seo Taiji to people in their 20s?

398
00:13:18,223 --> 00:13:20,293
- They don't know who he is. - They don't.

399
00:13:20,493 --> 00:13:21,992
- People in their 20s... - Is he that obscure?

400
00:13:21,993 --> 00:13:23,123
No.

401
00:13:23,923 --> 00:13:25,062
- Be careful. - No one knows him.

402
00:13:25,063 --> 00:13:26,222
People in their 20s don't know who Seo Taiji is.

403
00:13:26,223 --> 00:13:27,392
That means Seon Min is not popular.

404
00:13:27,393 --> 00:13:28,492
- That's true. - Really? Why?

405
00:13:28,493 --> 00:13:29,932
- Back in my day, he was the bomb. - Listen.

406
00:13:29,933 --> 00:13:31,302
- You're not in your 20s now. - That was when we were in our 20s.

407
00:13:31,303 --> 00:13:32,802
- That was when we were in our 20s. - He's as famous as H.O.T...

408
00:13:32,803 --> 00:13:34,703
when we were in our 20s.

409
00:13:34,873 --> 00:13:36,543
- Seon Min is trending these days. - Exactly.

410
00:13:36,673 --> 00:13:37,842
- He's super popular. - He's the most popular comedian.

411
00:13:37,843 --> 00:13:39,172
- He's the most popular now. - I was so surprised.

412
00:13:39,173 --> 00:13:41,073
(Min's popularity is a sensation.)

413
00:13:41,373 --> 00:13:43,913
- Jang Mi. Thank you. - Thank you.

414
00:13:44,013 --> 00:13:45,342
- Sell a lot. Thank you. - Have a good day.

415
00:13:45,343 --> 00:13:47,213
(He finally leaves the stall.)

416
00:13:47,483 --> 00:13:49,182
- Gosh, I love traditional markets. - Aren't they great?

417
00:13:49,183 --> 00:13:50,283
- Yes. - They're nice, right?

418
00:13:50,683 --> 00:13:52,653
- They recognized me. - How great is that?

419
00:13:52,883 --> 00:13:54,352
- Let's go. - Did we buy everything?

420
00:13:54,353 --> 00:13:55,592
- We got everything. - Let's go.

421
00:13:55,593 --> 00:13:56,663
Let's go.

422
00:13:57,293 --> 00:13:58,792
To the left. What a charming market.

423
00:13:58,793 --> 00:13:59,933
What a lively market.

424
00:14:00,193 --> 00:14:03,303
Seon Min, you were super popular at the market.

425
00:14:03,333 --> 00:14:05,263
I was so surprised. I mean it.

426
00:14:05,833 --> 00:14:09,033
(They arrive at Hwan's place in no time.)

427
00:14:09,203 --> 00:14:10,873
- Gosh. - Thank you.

428
00:14:11,643 --> 00:14:13,273
Welcome to my house.

429
00:14:13,973 --> 00:14:15,043
Gosh, this is nice.

430
00:14:15,213 --> 00:14:17,282
All right. Okay. Thank you.

431
00:14:17,283 --> 00:14:18,713
(Giving Hwan the groceries)

432
00:14:21,113 --> 00:14:22,153
Okay.

433
00:14:22,353 --> 00:14:23,582
- What's that? Gosh. - What is that?

434
00:14:23,583 --> 00:14:24,953
- The Bulgarian bag. - Why did you bring that?

435
00:14:26,023 --> 00:14:27,492
(He puts the Bulgarian bag around his neck with some struggle.)

436
00:14:27,493 --> 00:14:28,493
Okay.

437
00:14:29,553 --> 00:14:30,793
Sung Hwan.

438
00:14:31,523 --> 00:14:33,662
- All the way to the fifth floor? - Let's go.

439
00:14:33,663 --> 00:14:35,093
(Do you think you can walk up to the 5th floor with that?)

440
00:14:35,563 --> 00:14:38,262
The thing is, there's no elevator in my building.

441
00:14:38,263 --> 00:14:39,973
- There's no elevator. - Neither does my building.

442
00:14:40,533 --> 00:14:41,533
My gosh.

443
00:14:41,833 --> 00:14:44,543
- Gosh, it's a 15kg bag. - Walking up is a good workout too.

444
00:14:44,803 --> 00:14:46,612
I worked out my legs when I walked up the stairs.

445
00:14:46,613 --> 00:14:47,613
My gosh.

446
00:14:47,614 --> 00:14:48,842
(He arrives on the 5th floor while working out his lower body.)

447
00:14:48,843 --> 00:14:49,883
This place looks hip.

448
00:14:50,443 --> 00:14:52,882
(Panting)

449
00:14:52,883 --> 00:14:53,983
My gosh.

450
00:14:54,713 --> 00:14:55,983
- Welcome. - Sung Hwan.

451
00:14:56,213 --> 00:14:57,983
Oh, my. Thank you.

452
00:14:59,453 --> 00:15:00,993
Goodness, your house looks clean.

453
00:15:01,723 --> 00:15:04,993
(Exhausted)

454
00:15:06,433 --> 00:15:08,692
- Put it over there. - Your house looks amazing.

455
00:15:08,693 --> 00:15:09,903
- Over there. - Okay.

456
00:15:10,633 --> 00:15:11,663
My gosh.

457
00:15:12,233 --> 00:15:15,133
By the way, why did you bring a Bulgarian bag?

458
00:15:15,233 --> 00:15:16,503
All right. There.

459
00:15:17,703 --> 00:15:19,203
This is for your workout.

460
00:15:19,973 --> 00:15:21,113
It's a housewarming present.

461
00:15:21,773 --> 00:15:24,643
What kind of lunatic gives a Bulgarian bag as a present?

462
00:15:24,913 --> 00:15:27,152
- Me. I gave one to Ju Seung. - My gosh.

463
00:15:27,153 --> 00:15:29,153
- Sung Hwan, it's still a present. - I'm that lunatic.

464
00:15:31,553 --> 00:15:33,022
- I gave one to Ju Seung. - Yes.

465
00:15:33,023 --> 00:15:34,192
- You did. - What's this?

466
00:15:34,193 --> 00:15:35,223
(Moomoo gave it to Ju Seung as well.)

467
00:15:35,423 --> 00:15:36,822
(A Bulgarian bag)

468
00:15:36,823 --> 00:15:38,063
Is that also 15kg?

469
00:15:38,193 --> 00:15:39,193
- Yes. - What's this?

470
00:15:39,194 --> 00:15:40,633
I gave it a lot of thought, though.

471
00:15:40,733 --> 00:15:43,332
I knew for sure that we would eat a lot that day.

472
00:15:43,333 --> 00:15:44,602
- I bought that, - Right.

473
00:15:44,603 --> 00:15:45,833
so it could help us digest.

474
00:15:46,473 --> 00:15:48,002
This will help you make a lot of money this year.

475
00:15:48,003 --> 00:15:50,003
- Sunflowers. - That's a good present.

476
00:15:50,043 --> 00:15:51,103
I have one too.

477
00:15:51,573 --> 00:15:55,713
People don't know, but Sung Hwan is particular about interior design.

478
00:15:55,873 --> 00:15:56,983
I see. This is nice.

479
00:15:57,583 --> 00:15:59,542
- Look at him. He's unhappy. - This is nice.

480
00:15:59,543 --> 00:16:01,082
- He wears his heart on his sleeve. - Look at his mouth.

481
00:16:01,083 --> 00:16:03,652
You know what? I really appreciate your thoughtfulness.

482
00:16:03,653 --> 00:16:05,722
- Sung Hwan, I've got one more. - Hey!

483
00:16:05,723 --> 00:16:06,992
(I've got one more.)

484
00:16:06,993 --> 00:16:08,092
- What is that? - Earlier...

485
00:16:08,093 --> 00:16:09,722
- I knew you were toying with me. - His reaction is different.

486
00:16:09,723 --> 00:16:12,623
- It's a handkerchief. - Really? Gosh, that's crazy.

487
00:16:12,723 --> 00:16:15,193
You mentioned a handkerchief earlier.

488
00:16:15,763 --> 00:16:16,903
It's a three-handkerchief set.

489
00:16:17,463 --> 00:16:19,302
(Hwan always carries this with him.)

490
00:16:19,303 --> 00:16:21,203
- It's an essential item for him. - Being confident...

491
00:16:22,233 --> 00:16:23,443
You're so sweet.

492
00:16:24,003 --> 00:16:26,072
- Thank you. - He used it that morning too.

493
00:16:26,073 --> 00:16:27,773
- You have the freshest meat. - That's nice. How thoughtful.

494
00:16:28,113 --> 00:16:30,243
I was happy when I saw you use a handkerchief.

495
00:16:30,383 --> 00:16:32,082
I love it. Hey, thank you.

496
00:16:32,083 --> 00:16:33,782
- You sweat a lot. - I sweat so much.

497
00:16:33,783 --> 00:16:36,283
- Use it well. Do you like it? - I love it.

498
00:16:36,653 --> 00:16:37,653
I brought it today.

499
00:16:38,523 --> 00:16:39,852
- It's the one he gave me. - I see.

500
00:16:39,853 --> 00:16:40,952
Really?

501
00:16:40,953 --> 00:16:42,592
- You're thoughtful. - Seriously.

502
00:16:42,593 --> 00:16:44,493
- You're Soo Jong among comedians. - How thoughtful.

503
00:16:46,023 --> 00:16:47,593
- Choi Soo Jong? - Choi Soo Jong.

504
00:16:48,563 --> 00:16:49,863
Let's go to the rooftop.

505
00:16:50,663 --> 00:16:51,733
I always wanted to visit.

506
00:16:52,163 --> 00:16:55,272
So many people are curious about my rooftop.

507
00:16:55,273 --> 00:16:57,643
My gosh. What an honor, Sung Hwan.

508
00:16:58,373 --> 00:17:00,172
Seon Min is the first one to visit Sung Hwan's house.

