I can eat anything. What's this? Let's have this.

2060
01:17:00,169 --> 01:17:01,409
Is it grilled meat?

2061
01:17:01,809 --> 01:17:03,309
It's pan-fried.

2062
01:17:03,639 --> 01:17:04,738
- Pan-fried? - What?

2063
01:17:04,739 --> 01:17:06,048
- What does that mean? - It's pan-fried.

2064
01:17:06,049 --> 01:17:08,749
(It means it's pan-fried.)

2065
01:17:08,819 --> 01:17:10,549
What seafood dishes do you have?

2066
01:17:10,949 --> 01:17:12,989
Is there a menu you'd like to recommend to us?

2067
01:17:13,119 --> 01:17:14,989
Is this the only spicy dish you have?

2068
01:17:16,689 --> 01:17:19,929
(Young Pyo orders in fluent Chinese.)

2069
01:17:19,959 --> 01:17:22,828
You really sound like a teacher now.

2070
01:17:22,829 --> 01:17:24,859
- Come on! - He really does.

2071
01:17:25,399 --> 01:17:27,668
You don't hesitate at all.

2072
01:17:27,669 --> 01:17:29,268
- I don't teach carelessly. - I know.

2073
01:17:29,269 --> 01:17:30,299
"Carelessly."

2074
01:17:30,869 --> 01:17:33,108
- "Carelessly." - "I don't teach carelessly."

2075
01:17:33,109 --> 01:17:35,169
Order a lot. Order everything you want to eat.

2076
01:17:35,909 --> 01:17:37,439
Why don't you have a glass of wine?

2077
01:17:37,579 --> 01:17:39,348
- Wine. - Really? Then...

2078
01:17:39,349 --> 01:17:40,378
Let's have this.

2079
01:17:40,379 --> 01:17:41,879
- Gosh, you're a successful friend. - This will be fine.

2080
01:17:42,149 --> 01:17:43,648
You say that a lot to the friends you feel grateful to...

2081
01:17:43,649 --> 01:17:45,178
- after making a lot of money. - Right.

2082
01:17:45,179 --> 01:17:47,088
- "Order everything you want." - That's right.

2083
01:17:47,089 --> 01:17:48,859
You'd say things like, "Tell me whatever you want to get."

2084
01:17:49,519 --> 01:17:50,988
(Staring)

2085
01:17:50,989 --> 01:17:52,659
Gosh, you're going to get a doctoral degree?

2086
01:17:53,589 --> 01:17:54,958
I can't believe it either.

2087
01:17:54,959 --> 01:17:56,329
(Embarrassed)

2088
01:17:56,899 --> 01:17:59,369
(Look how much we've grown.)

2089
01:18:00,229 --> 01:18:01,669
What do you teach, then?

2090
01:18:01,899 --> 01:18:02,968
It's something like this.

2091
01:18:02,969 --> 01:18:04,738
You teach? What do you know?

2092
01:18:04,739 --> 01:18:06,638
- I pretend to know. - Exactly. What do you teach?

2093
01:18:06,639 --> 01:18:08,068
- They're true friends. - You teach in Korean?

2094
01:18:08,069 --> 01:18:09,278
A conversation between true friends.

2095
01:18:09,279 --> 01:18:11,439
I teach Korean, basically.

2096
01:18:12,209 --> 01:18:14,449
Don't you need to speak in standard Korean to teach Korean?

2097
01:18:15,079 --> 01:18:17,278
I speak like this because I'm with you.

2098
01:18:17,279 --> 01:18:18,889
I'm really good at standard Korean.

2099
01:18:20,389 --> 01:18:21,688
- Seriously. - That's dirty.

2100
01:18:21,689 --> 01:18:22,958
- "That's dirty." - Totally dirty.

2101
01:18:22,959 --> 01:18:25,388
Seriously. I'm really good at standard Korean.

2102
01:18:25,389 --> 01:18:26,559
(Firm)

2103
01:18:26,689 --> 01:18:28,758
I can't be like this to the Chinese students.

2104
01:18:28,759 --> 01:18:31,859
"Gosh, what shall we learn today?"

2105
01:18:32,129 --> 01:18:34,169
(That's true.)

2106
01:18:34,529 --> 01:18:36,039
You're amazing.

2107
01:18:36,199 --> 01:18:38,099
You became a teacher in China.

2108
01:18:38,299 --> 01:18:39,838
- And one became a singer. - I still can't believe it.

2109
01:18:39,839 --> 01:18:40,939
- It feels like a dream. - And one became a teacher.

2110
01:18:41,609 --> 01:18:42,838
I am amazing too.

2111
01:18:42,839 --> 01:18:43,938
You're friends who remember...

2112
01:18:43,939 --> 01:18:44,939
- each other's lousy sides. - Yes.

2113
01:18:44,940 --> 01:18:46,948
It must feel weird to see one another's success.

2114
01:18:46,949 --> 01:18:47,949
- It must feel weird. - Right.

2115
01:18:47,949 --> 01:18:48,949
That's right.

2116
01:18:49,019 --> 01:18:50,878
By the way, where did you buy your clothes?

2117
01:18:50,879 --> 01:18:52,119
Yes.

2118
01:18:52,219 --> 01:18:53,719
Did someone style you?

2119
01:18:54,049 --> 01:18:55,248
No, I did it myself.

2120
01:18:55,249 --> 01:18:57,319
- Goodness, you learned? - I chose them myself.

2121
01:18:57,659 --> 01:18:59,229
- I did. - From who?

2122
01:19:00,859 --> 01:19:03,098
- Do you know who CODE KUNST is? - You look nice.

2123
01:19:03,099 --> 01:19:05,298
- "Do you know who CODE KUNST is?" - "Do you know who CODE KUNST is?"

2124
01:19:05,299 --> 01:19:06,599
(Smiling)

2125
01:19:07,029 --> 01:19:08,328
Since he's my fashion guru.

2126
01:19:08,329 --> 01:19:09,399
Of course.

2127
01:19:09,869 --> 01:19:11,769
- He dresses well. - That's right.

2128
01:19:11,999 --> 01:19:14,639
You know CODE KUNST dresses well too?

2129
01:19:14,709 --> 01:19:15,779
Of course.

2130
01:19:16,139 --> 01:19:19,078
If I look at you like this,

2131
01:19:19,079 --> 01:19:20,709
you look like...

2132
01:19:20,879 --> 01:19:23,978
- Seo In Guk a little. - What is it?

2133
01:19:23,979 --> 01:19:25,049
(Me?)

2134
01:19:25,479 --> 01:19:27,088
(Smiling from ear to ear)

2135
01:19:27,089 --> 01:19:28,649
You're so happy about it.

2136
01:19:28,919 --> 01:19:31,459
Seeing you smiling like that,

2137
01:19:31,659 --> 01:19:34,459
you look a bit...

2138
01:19:34,589 --> 01:19:36,158
You look a bit foolish.

2139
01:19:36,159 --> 01:19:38,458
(You look a bit foolish.)

2140
01:19:38,459 --> 01:19:39,969
- You're giving off that vibe. - Is that so?

2141
01:19:40,769 --> 01:19:43,039
- You two look really close. - Right.

2142
01:19:43,199 --> 01:19:44,768
You care about each other too.

2143
01:19:44,769 --> 01:19:46,569
- And you offend each other a bit. - Right.

2144
01:19:48,739 --> 01:19:51,039
(The dishes are served 1 by 1 while they catch up.)

2145
01:19:52,749 --> 01:19:54,108
- Isn't it delicious? - Yes.

2146
01:19:54,109 --> 01:19:56,549
(Pouring)

2147
01:19:57,619 --> 01:19:58,888
(Impressed)

2148
01:19:58,889 --> 01:20:00,649
- She poured it. - What is that?

2149
01:20:03,459 --> 01:20:05,288
- Have you ever seen that? - What is that?

2150
01:20:05,289 --> 01:20:06,329
It's no joke.

2151
01:20:06,429 --> 01:20:08,188
- It's a decanter. - The flavor changes.

2152
01:20:08,189 --> 01:20:10,028
- How can it be possible? - As it meets oxygen.

2153
01:20:10,029 --> 01:20:12,199
Oh, then the flavor becomes richer?

2154
01:20:12,929 --> 01:20:13,969
Aerating.

2155
01:20:14,399 --> 01:20:15,569
Gosh, it's to die for.

2156
01:20:16,239 --> 01:20:17,369
It's to die for.

2157
01:20:17,969 --> 01:20:19,738
My gosh. I didn't know the glass would be this big.

2158
01:20:19,739 --> 01:20:20,739
- My goodness. - I know.

2159
01:20:21,839 --> 01:20:23,579
- So? Shall we clink our glasses? - It's as big as my face.

2160
01:20:23,709 --> 01:20:24,908
- We should clink, right? - It's needless to say.

2161
01:20:24,909 --> 01:20:25,909
Of course, we should clink our glasses.

2162
01:20:26,779 --> 01:20:28,509
My gosh. The sound is amazing too.

2163
01:20:28,949 --> 01:20:30,419
It's amazing, isn't it?

2164
01:20:30,479 --> 01:20:32,119
- I know. - Seriously.

2165
01:20:33,489 --> 01:20:36,188
Gosh, Ji Hyeon, you're so cool. You became successful...

2166
01:20:36,189 --> 01:20:38,289
and had wine in Shanghai.

2167
01:20:38,689 --> 01:20:40,759
With a background like that.

2168
01:20:41,329 --> 01:20:42,359
I've made it.

2169
01:20:44,599 --> 01:20:45,828
(Knocking)

2170
01:20:45,829 --> 01:20:47,129
- Someone else is here. - What?

2171
01:20:47,669 --> 01:20:48,828
What's that? What did you order?

2172
01:20:48,829 --> 01:20:50,439
Oh, it must be their food.

2173
01:20:51,599 --> 01:20:53,668
- It's incredible. - Gosh.

2174
01:20:53,669 --> 01:20:54,939
- What is that? - Oh, my.

2175
01:20:55,639 --> 01:20:56,808
Oh, my.

2176
01:20:56,809 --> 01:20:58,409
- It's huge. - I know.

2177
01:21:00,949 --> 01:21:02,878
- It's lobster. That's right. - The food...

2178
01:21:02,879 --> 01:21:04,318
- It's no joke. - It's lobster.

2179
01:21:04,319 --> 01:21:05,748
It's stir-fried lobster.

2180
01:21:05,749 --> 01:21:07,189
Gosh, look at all this meat.

2181
01:21:08,919 --> 01:21:09,988
It's amazing.

2182
01:21:09,989 --> 01:21:12,019
- It's the steak we ordered earlier. - Is it steak?

2183
01:21:14,089 --> 01:21:16,128
It's a must to order a steak and a lobster.

2184
01:21:16,129 --> 01:21:17,129
That's right.

2185
01:21:17,130 --> 01:21:19,499
When you treat a meal for your friend after becoming successful.

2186
01:21:20,899 --> 01:21:22,298
(What do you think?)

2187
01:21:22,299 --> 01:21:23,969
- It's huge. - I know.

2188
01:21:24,069 --> 01:21:28,568
Do you think they cooked the head as well?

2189
01:21:28,569 --> 01:21:32,208
Or do you think it's just for decoration?

2190
01:21:32,209 --> 01:21:33,378
- It's for decoration. - Right?

2191
01:21:33,379 --> 01:21:34,679
It's for decoration.

2192
01:21:35,509 --> 01:21:37,148
- Right? - It looks like they reuse this.

2193
01:21:37,149 --> 01:21:39,089
I think they use it for decoration.

2194
01:21:39,319 --> 01:21:41,389
But the roe... Look. It's huge.

2195
01:21:42,589 --> 01:21:44,119
- That's for decoration. - They just cooked it.

2196
01:21:44,359 --> 01:21:46,229
- They just cooked it. - "They just cooked it."

2197
01:21:46,429 --> 01:21:47,458
That's right. They just...

2198
01:21:47,459 --> 01:21:48,528
- cooked the alive one. - Yes.

2199
01:21:48,529 --> 01:21:50,358
- They must've cooked it. - It's real.

2200
01:21:50,359 --> 01:21:51,958
- Gosh, there's meat in here too. - That's right.

2201
01:21:51,959 --> 01:21:53,928
- See inside here. - It was freshly caught.

2202
01:21:53,929 --> 01:21:55,969
They scraped the meat out of it for the dish.

2203
01:21:56,199 --> 01:21:57,238
My goodness.

2204
01:21:57,239 --> 01:21:58,498
We should try a bite...

2205
01:21:58,499 --> 01:21:59,769
- since it's served, right? - Yes, we should.

2206
01:21:59,969 --> 01:22:01,569
Right? Let's have the big piece.

2207
01:22:02,169 --> 01:22:03,239
This is amazing.

2208
01:22:03,539 --> 01:22:05,639
- Look how plump it is. - It must be delicious.

2209
01:22:06,479 --> 01:22:07,508
My goodness.

2210
01:22:07,509 --> 01:22:08,509
(Gulping)

2211
01:22:08,510 --> 01:22:10,949
(Taking a bite)

2212
01:22:12,819 --> 01:22:15,149
(Impressed)

2213
01:22:15,519 --> 01:22:16,718
(Amazed)

2214
01:22:16,719 --> 01:22:19,089
Hey, it's bouncy.

2215
01:22:19,759 --> 01:22:20,829
You're right.

2216
01:22:22,599 --> 01:22:24,158
- Shall we cut it? - Yes, we shall.

2217
01:22:24,159 --> 01:22:25,199
My goodness.

2218
01:22:25,999 --> 01:22:27,028
It's different.

2219
01:22:27,029 --> 01:22:29,168
(Cutting)

2220
01:22:29,169 --> 01:22:30,239
It's somewhat different.

2221
01:22:30,969 --> 01:22:32,869
- He's cutting it. - It feels different.

2222
01:22:34,309 --> 01:22:35,369
It's no joke.

2223
01:22:36,309 --> 01:22:38,179
The marbling is no joke.

2224
01:22:40,379 --> 01:22:42,048
(Impressed)

2225
01:22:42,049 --> 01:22:43,619
- Is it so good? - It's good, right?

2226
01:22:43,749 --> 01:22:44,778
It's delicious.

2227
01:22:44,779 --> 01:22:47,149
(It's delicious.)

2228
01:22:47,589 --> 01:22:49,788
They look like kids who are quickly eating food...

2229
01:22:49,789 --> 01:22:51,519
before the rich owner of the house comes back home.

2230
01:22:52,459 --> 01:22:54,859
"Hurry up and eat! We don't have much time."

2231
01:22:56,099 --> 01:22:57,529
- "They're coming!" - They're so cute.

2232
01:23:00,029 --> 01:23:01,529
- Have a drink. - Gosh, this is nice.

2233
01:23:03,169 --> 01:23:06,209
I was really happy because my friend seemed happy.

2234
01:23:06,739 --> 01:23:07,769
I know.

2235
01:23:07,869 --> 01:23:09,839
That's how it was.

2236
01:23:12,309 --> 01:23:14,909
I got you something.

2237
01:23:15,379 --> 01:23:17,379
- What is it? - What did you get?

2238
01:23:19,349 --> 01:23:21,119
I got you this.

2239
01:23:21,589 --> 01:23:23,219
Don't make me excited.

2240
01:23:23,319 --> 01:23:24,559
I got you this.

2241
01:23:24,989 --> 01:23:26,059
For real?

2242
01:23:28,059 --> 01:23:29,099
Here.

2243
01:23:29,699 --> 01:23:31,098
I hope you'll get your doctoral degree.

2244
01:23:31,099 --> 01:23:32,668
(A gift Ji Hyeon got him to root for his success in doctoral degree)

2245
01:23:32,669 --> 01:23:34,669
I didn't get you anything.

2246
01:23:36,699 --> 01:23:38,039
For real, this is...

2247
01:23:38,739 --> 01:23:40,439
- What is it? - What is it?

2248
01:23:40,839 --> 01:23:42,508
- What is it? - What is that?

2249
01:23:42,509 --> 01:23:43,579
(Curious)

2250
01:23:46,749 --> 01:23:47,749
My gosh.

2251
01:23:47,750 --> 01:23:49,348
- Honestly... - Yes.

2252
01:23:49,349 --> 01:23:51,719
- I looked forward to it a little. - I didn't write anything.

2253
01:23:53,149 --> 01:23:54,818
- Gosh. - A letter between two men?

2254
01:23:54,819 --> 01:23:56,258
You don't write letters to your true friend.

2255
01:23:56,259 --> 01:23:57,458
- I know. - It'll give me goosebumps.

2256
01:23:57,459 --> 01:23:58,459
That's right.

2257
01:23:58,559 --> 01:24:00,558
- I thought I'd see something. - You think I'm crazy?

2258
01:24:00,559 --> 01:24:02,798
(You think I'm crazy?)

2259
01:24:02,799 --> 01:24:04,158
- That's real. - It's so real.

2260
01:24:04,159 --> 01:24:05,558
- It is real. - "You think I'm crazy?"

2261
01:24:05,559 --> 01:24:06,629
He meant it.

2262
01:24:07,329 --> 01:24:08,528
- A fountain pen. - Right.

2263
01:24:08,529 --> 01:24:09,568
It's not a fountain pen.

2264
01:24:09,569 --> 01:24:10,598
- It's a ballpoint pen. - A ballpoint pen?

2265
01:24:10,599 --> 01:24:12,299
I was going to get you a fountain pen.

2266
01:24:12,439 --> 01:24:14,308
Fountain pens are inconvenient.

2267
01:24:14,309 --> 01:24:16,409
- You have to keep filling the ink. - You can never use it.

2268
01:24:16,879 --> 01:24:18,538
I thought you wouldn't use a fountain pen.

2269
01:24:18,539 --> 01:24:20,179
You need to keep refilling ink.

2270
01:24:20,409 --> 01:24:21,548
Y. P. Yoon.

2271
01:24:21,549 --> 01:24:24,319
I engraved your name too. Isn't it cool?

2272
01:24:25,079 --> 01:24:27,649
Gosh, thank you so much.

2273
01:24:27,689 --> 01:24:29,758
(Pleased)

2274
01:24:29,759 --> 01:24:31,919
I'll make sure to use this.

2275
01:24:32,419 --> 01:24:34,188
After writing the thesis for my doctoral degree,

2276
01:24:34,189 --> 01:24:36,198
I'll use this to sign it.

2277
01:24:36,199 --> 01:24:37,958
I'll let my name show.

2278
01:24:37,959 --> 01:24:40,798
Before I get the degree...

2279
01:24:40,799 --> 01:24:42,998
Even I feel moved. I feel proud for him.

2280
01:24:42,999 --> 01:24:44,938
I'll show the side that has my name.

2281
01:24:44,939 --> 01:24:46,208
- All right. - Thank you.

2282
01:24:46,209 --> 01:24:47,609
Thank you so much.

2283
01:24:47,739 --> 01:24:48,969
Make sure to get the doctoral degree.

2284
01:24:49,609 --> 01:24:50,639
Seriously.

2285
01:24:50,939 --> 01:24:53,609
Come again next time. I'm serious. I'm not joking.

2286
01:24:53,709 --> 01:24:56,178
- Goodness. - Thanks for coming.

2287
01:24:56,179 --> 01:24:57,378
- I'll treat you to a meal. - Get the doctoral degree, okay?

2288
01:24:57,379 --> 01:24:58,479
I really will.

2289
01:25:00,419 --> 01:25:02,988
The day I spent in Shanghai...

2290
01:25:02,989 --> 01:25:04,989
(The day I spent in Shanghai...)

2291
01:25:06,389 --> 01:25:09,199
I had a lot of mixed feelings.

2292
01:25:10,029 --> 01:25:12,599
If my past self from 20 years ago...

2293
01:25:13,529 --> 01:25:15,329
appeared before me today,

2294
01:25:16,469 --> 01:25:17,669
I think...

2295
01:25:18,499 --> 01:25:20,909
I'd have been emotional.

2296
01:25:21,809 --> 01:25:24,008
"What would've happened if I hadn't gone to China?"

2297
01:25:24,009 --> 01:25:25,579
I had such thoughts.

2298
01:25:26,109 --> 01:25:28,609
"What if my parents' businesses had done well?"

2299
01:25:28,779 --> 01:25:31,648
But I became a singer...

2300
01:25:31,649 --> 01:25:33,648
because they went bankrupt.

2301
01:25:33,649 --> 01:25:34,688
You never know what life has in store.

2302
01:25:34,689 --> 01:25:36,789
So it's okay.

2303
01:25:37,459 --> 01:25:38,919
It's just part of my memory.

2304
01:25:39,589 --> 01:25:41,828
Looking back, the bad things that happened to us...

2305
01:25:41,829 --> 01:25:43,059
became memories now.

2306
01:25:43,229 --> 01:25:45,968
- It's a good memory. - He grew up to be amazing.

2307
01:25:45,969 --> 01:25:47,299
(Everything that's gone by becomes a cherished memory.)

2308
01:25:48,329 --> 01:25:50,198
You should be the World Star.

2309
01:25:50,199 --> 01:25:51,898
No, that's too much.

2310
01:25:51,899 --> 01:25:56,378
(Shanghai Carries the Memories)

2311
01:25:56,379 --> 01:25:57,979
(Next story)

2312
01:25:58,139 --> 01:26:02,819
(Hye Young kept her pace and was relaxed.)

2313
01:26:03,679 --> 01:26:07,189
